.TH PKI\-HTTPD 8 2026-11-20 "Peios pki 0.1.0"
.SH NAME
pki\-httpd \- serve the CRLs the Peios certificate authority publishes over HTTP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pki\-httpd
.br
.B pki\-httpd
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help | \-V | \-\-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pki\-httpd
serves the certificate revocation lists (CRLs) that
.BR pkid (8)
publishes, so that software checking revocation can fetch each one from the address its CA's certificates name.
.PP
peinit starts
.B pki\-httpd
as the
.B pki\-httpd
service, under its own virtual service account; you do not run it yourself.
It refuses to start under any other identity.
It holds no keys and cannot reach
.BR pkid :
it only reads the folder
.B pkid
publishes to, so a fault in it exposes nothing but the CRLs, which are public.
.PP
.B pkid
writes each CRL under
.I /var/state/pki/http
at the path of each of its CA's http distribution points, and
.B pki\-httpd
serves that path: the CRL for
.B http://pki.home/crl/issuing.crl
is served as
.BR /crl/issuing.crl ,
whichever host name the request used.
.PP
It answers one GET or HEAD request per connection and then closes it.
A path is served only if every segment is letters, digits,
.BR . ,
.BR _ ,
.B \-
or
.BR ~ ,
not starting with
.BR . ,
and names a regular file; anything else is not found.
A query is ignored.
Any other method is refused, as is a request whose head exceeds 8 KiB, or that takes more than 10 seconds.
At most 64 connections are served at once; more are closed straight away.
CRLs are served as
.BR application/pkix\-crl .
.SH OPTIONS
.B pki\-httpd
takes no options when it serves.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the program name and version and exit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.B pki\-httpd
listens on every address, on the TCP port
.B Machine\eSoftware\ePki\eHttp Port
sets, 80 by default, read when it starts.
Binding the port needs a reservation granting it, which
.B pki setup
adds; see
.BR pki (8).
Run
.B regman Machine\eSoftware\ePki\eHttp
for the value.
.SH SECURITY
The service account may read
.I /var/state/pki/http
and
.BR Machine\eSoftware\ePki\eHttp ,
and bind its port, and nothing else
.B pki setup
grants it.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Help or the version was printed, or the listener closed.
.TP
.B 1
.B pki\-httpd
could not start: it runs under the wrong identity, its port setting is not valid, or it cannot listen on the port.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error: an argument was given.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/state/pki/http
The CRLs served.
.SH READINESS
.B pki\-httpd
tells peinit it is ready once it is listening.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR regman (1),
.BR pki (8),
.BR pkid (8)
.PP
https://learn.peios.org/peios/using-peios/certificate-authority/overview
